Program 11 — Steps to Execute
Aim

To create a CI/CD pipeline using Azure DevOps with a self-hosted agent and simulate deployment using YAML pipelines.

Requirements
Java installed
Maven installed
Git installed
GitHub account
Azure DevOps account
Self-hosted agent configured
Step 1: Create Maven Project

Open CMD and run:

mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=demoapp -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DinteractiveMode=false

Move into project:

cd demoapp

Check files:

dir

You should see:

pom.xml
src
Step 2: Initialize Git Repository

Run:

git init
git add .
git commit -m "Maven project"
Step 3: Create GitHub Repository

Go to:

GitHub

Create repository:

demoapp
Step 4: Push Project to GitHub

Connect remote repository:

git remote add origin https://github.com/Nagashreemurthy21/demoapp.git

Push files:

git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
Step 5: Create Azure DevOps Project

Open:

Azure DevOps

Create new project:

Program11
Step 6: Configure Self-Hosted Agent

Go to:

Project Settings
→ Agent Pools

Create pool:

NagashreeAgent

Download Windows agent ZIP.

Extract to:

C:\azureagent
Step 7: Configure Agent

Open CMD inside agent folder:

config.cmd

Provide:

Server URL
https://dev.azure.com/Vtu-devops-org
Authentication Type
PAT
Pool Name
NagashreeAgent
Step 8: Start Agent

Run:

.\run.cmd

You should see:

Listening for Jobs
Step 9: Install Maven

Add Maven bin path to Environment Variables:

C:\Program Files\apache-maven-3.9.15-bin\apache-maven-3.9.15\bin

Verify Maven:

mvn -version
Step 10: Create YAML Pipeline File

Inside project folder create:

azure-pipelines.yml

Add this code:

trigger:
- main

pool:
  name: NagashreeAgent

steps:
- task: Maven@3
  inputs:
    mavenPomFile: 'pom.xml'
    goals: 'package'

- script: |
    echo "Simulating deployment..."
    mkdir deployed
    copy target\*.jar deployed\
    echo "Deployment successful!"
  displayName: 'Simulate Deployment'

- script: |
    echo "Contents of deployed folder:"
    dir deployed
  displayName: 'Verify Deployment Output'
Step 11: Push YAML File

Run:

git add .
git commit -m "Added pipeline YAML"
git push origin main
Step 12: Create Azure Pipeline

Go to:

Pipelines
→ Create Pipeline

Select:

GitHub

Choose repository:

demoapp

Select:

Existing Azure Pipelines YAML file

Choose:

azure-pipelines.yml
Step 13: Run Pipeline

Click:

Run Pipeline

Then:

Run
Step 14: Verify Output

Pipeline should show green tick ✅

Check deployment folder:

C:\azureagent\vsts-agent-win-x64-4.273.0\_work\1\s\deployed

You should see:

.jar file
Result

CI/CD pipeline using Azure DevOps and self-hosted agent was successfully created and deployment simulation was completed successfully.
